# apps/api/.dev.vars — local dev secrets for the Cloudflare Worker.
#
# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` (gitignored), fill in real values, then run:
#   bun run dev
#
# Wrangler reads `.dev.vars` automatically and exposes each KEY=VALUE on `c.env`
# inside the Worker. The same file is uploaded as production Worker secrets
# during `bun --filter @app/api run deploy` (or `bun --filter @app/api run secrets:put`).
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# AES-GCM key used to encrypt Drive OAuth refresh tokens at rest in D1.
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -base64 32
# (32 random bytes, base64-encoded — that's 44 chars ending in '='.)
# The Worker refuses to start in non-test environments without this set.
OAUTH_TOKEN_KEY_BASE64=

# HMAC-SHA256 key used to sign the `tenex_sid` session cookie that pins a
# browser to a UserId for 14 days after Drive sign-in. Distinct from
# OAUTH_TOKEN_KEY_BASE64 (different algorithm, different concern: this one
# never touches Drive tokens). Generate a fresh one with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# The Worker refuses to start in non-test environments without this set —
# missing key would silently de-auth every request.
SESSION_SIGNING_KEY=

# Google OAuth client for Drive ingestion.
# Create one at https://console.cloud.google.com → APIs & Services → Credentials:
#   1. New OAuth client ID → Web application.
#   2. Authorized redirect URI: http://localhost:8787/rpc/ingestion/authCallback
#      (add your prod URL here too once deployed).
#   3. Enable Drive API, Docs API, Sheets API, Slides API for the project.
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT=http://localhost:8787/rpc/ingestion/authCallback

# OpenRouter API key. The wiki compiler, the chat agent loop, the
# verification linter, AND the chat embeddings adapter all read from
# this one key. OpenRouter ships an OpenAI-compatible embeddings
# endpoint at `/api/v1/embeddings`, so the chat semantic-search fallback
# (Vectorize-backed `searchSources` + `searchWiki`) reuses this same
# key — no separate OpenAI account needed. Get one at
# https://openrouter.ai/keys.
#
# Embedding model: `openai/text-embedding-3-small` (1536-dim, cosine —
# matches the `tenex-sources` Vectorize index declared in wrangler.toml).
# Missing the VECTORIZE binding on the account → chat falls back to D1
# token overlap with zero behavior change.
OPEN_ROUTER_API_KEY=

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Comma-separated list of web origins the OAuth callback is allowed to 302
# back to after a successful Drive sign-in. Defends against open-redirect
# from a tampered `returnTo`. Falls back to the request's own origin when
# unset, which is correct for single-origin local dev (vite proxies /rpc to
# the api on :8787).
# WEB_APP_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Observability (optional — every LLM call + top-level use-case emits OTel
# spans regardless of what you set here)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Default: no env vars → ConsoleTracer writes one structured JSON line per
# finished span to stdout (visible via `wrangler tail` or in dev console).
# That's enough to inspect spans without any external account.
#
# Langfuse-ready: set the three LANGFUSE_* vars and the OTLP exporter
# auto-derives the endpoint (`${LANGFUSE_HOST}/api/public/otel/v1/traces`)
# and `Authorization: Basic base64(public:secret)` header. Sign up + get
# keys at https://cloud.langfuse.com (or self-host).
# LANGFUSE_HOST=https://cloud.langfuse.com
# LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=pk-lf-…
# LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=sk-lf-…
#
# Generic OTLP/HTTP backends (Honeycomb, Grafana Cloud, Tempo, anything
# OTel-aware): set the endpoint that EXCLUDES the trailing `/v1/traces` —
# the exporter appends it. Headers are W3C-style "k=v,k2=v2".
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=https://api.honeycomb.io
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=x-honeycomb-team=YOUR_API_KEY
